  'prompt.makeup.text': 'Create a professional makeup guide infographic from the portrait photo I attached, framed 9:16 and laid out like a modern beauty-magazine feature. Keep her real features, skin tone and bone structure recognisable — no reshaping, no slimming, no plastic retouching. Show the finished makeup large, with a few close detail call-outs around it — a winged eyeliner eye, a soft rose blush cheek and a satin pink lip — each pointing at the real area of the same face, hair pulled back, soft even light, plain light background. Prioritise the visuals: at most three short labels, no paragraphs, no watermark.',
  'prompt.hair.title': 'Hairstyle changer',
  'prompt.hair.description': 'Try a new cut on your own photo: describe it, or attach a reference picture.',
  'prompt.hair.text': 'The first photo I attached is me: restyle only my hair, the way a hairdresser would preview it. Keep the face, expression, skin, age, head angle, framing and background exactly as they are. If I attached a second photo, that is the cut I want — match its length, shape, layering and colour; if not, use this description: a soft collarbone-length cut with long face-framing layers and a slightly darker root melt. Salon-quality finish either way: shape and movement, healthy shine, a natural hairline and roots growing from the scalp, a few loose strands, believable even colour. Do not slim or reshape the face, do not add makeup, no text or watermark.',
